d to go to the Analytics dashboard, Add the site to the analytics and <i>then</i> disable the snippet. I find this approach entirely invasive, you should opt-in to features like that not have to opt-out. Just a warning out there to folks who might not be aware of this."},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Tell HN: Cloudflare silently injects its analytics when you switch nameservers"}},"_tags":["story","author_stagas","story_49322107","ask_hn","front_page"],"author":"stagas","children":[49322686,49322712,49322763,49322782,49322818,49322833,49322864,49322910,49322913,49322934,49322970,49323016,49323191,49323216,49323239,49323333,49323462,49323481,49323557,49323613,49323734,49323755,49323768,49323811,49323848,49324118,49325105],"created_at":"2026-08-16T17:49:46Z","created_at_i":1786902586,"num_comments":60,"objectID":"49322107","points":253,"story_id":49322107,"story_text":"A few hours ago I switched my nameservers to Cloudflare in order to enable R2 bucket serving through my own subdomain, and I found out that it silently had injected a JS analytics snippet in my HTML-only JS-free site textlog.cc \u2014 I had to go to the Analytics dashboard, Add the site to the analytics and <i>then</i> disable the snippet. I find this approach entirely invasive, you should opt-in to features like that not have to opt-out. Just a warning out there to folks who might not be aware of this.","title":"Tell HN: Cloudflare silently injects its analytics when you switch nameservers","updated_at":"2026-08-17T00:27:29Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"hruvhwe"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Models Are Getting Dumber on Purpose"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://w4g1.dev/blog/models-are-getting-dumber-on-purpose"}},"_tags":["story","author_hruvhwe","story_49322695","front_page"],"author":"hruvhwe","children":[49323056,49323060,49323070,49323072,49323097,49323113,49323137,